      "category": "statistical_arbitrage",
      "trading_idea": "Quarterly disclosures contain a multivariate operating-state update rather than a single earnings number: revenue, margins, cash conversion, working-capital items, and dilution tend to move along persistent industry-specific economic directions. Investors often react to the salient headline surprise while underweighting whether the full accounting update is a coherent, high-quality transition; a fundamentally favorable transition with an unusually muted initial price response should continue to reprice, with the converse for unfavorable transitions. The hypothesis is falsified if return continuation is absent after conditioning on the signed accounting-state projection and initial reaction deficit; it may persist because processing a multidimensional filing is costly and headline-driven discretionary and systematic traders dominate the first days after disclosure.",
      "description": "At each point-in-time fundamental update, form a standardized vector of changes in revenue, gross margin, operating margin, operating cash flow, receivables, inventory, and shares outstanding. Estimate the causal industry cross-sectional principal direction of recent accounting updates, project each firm's update onto that direction, and score the signed gap between this coherent operating-state innovation and its contemporaneous short-window price response; rank the residual cross-sectionally.",
