      "category": "mean_reversion",
      "trading_idea": "Bubble-driven phase transitions are characterized less by high returns alone than by accelerating trend, shrinking spacing between directional excursions, and increasingly synchronized volume participation. Such paths attract trend-following and performance-chasing capital until marginal buyers are exhausted, at which point a short-horizon reversal becomes likely. The idea fails if accelerating, geometrically compressed price-volume paths remain more persistent than comparable non-compressed trends after controlling for ordinary momentum.",
